<!--
  iOS usage strings and background modes.

  These go into ios/App/App/Info.plist after `pnpm cap:add:ios`. Kept here for the same reason as
  the Android manifest: the generated project is not committed, and these strings are the ones
  Apple shows to a driver in the permission prompt. Reconstructing them from memory during a
  release is how a fleet ends up asking for the driver's location with the default placeholder
  text — which App Review rejects, and which deserves rejecting.

  ABOUT THE WORDING

  The usage strings are in Bulgarian because that is who this is deployed to today, and because a
  permission prompt is worthless in a language the person reading it does not use. They say what
  is recorded, when, and when it stops. They do not say "to improve your experience".

  UIBackgroundModes: `location` only. Not `fetch`, not `processing`. The app has exactly one
  reason to run in the background and no business doing anything else there.
-->

<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
<string>AYtracker записва маршрута ви, докато сте на смяна. Записът започва, когато започнете смяна, и спира, когато я приключите.</string>

<key>NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
<string>За да се запише целият маршрут, включително когато екранът е заключен, AYtracker се нуждае от достъп „Винаги“. Записва се само по време на смяна или курс — никога извън тях.</string>

<key>NSLocationAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
<string>За да се запише целият маршрут, включително когато екранът е заключен, AYtracker се нуждае от достъп „Винаги“. Записва се само по време на смяна или курс — никога извън тях.</string>

<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
<array>
    <string>location</string>
</array>

<!--
  App Transport Security is left at its default: no exceptions, no arbitrary loads. The portal is
  HTTPS. A tracking app with an ATS exception is a tracking app whose location stream can be read
  on any café network.
-->
